WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 0: Alphabet & Sounds.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.120
Who This Is For ESL students aged 5–7 years.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.540
Absolute beginners with limited or
no knowledge of the English alphabet.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.660
Children preparing to enter Cambridge Global English Year 1.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:24.620
What Children Will Be Able to Do In this short lecture,
preview the key ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

6
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.480
By the end of this unit, you will be able to learner
can recognise and name uppercase and lowercase letters.

7
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.140
you will also learner can connect
letters a-z with their most common sounds.

8
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.420
you will also learner can hear and
say beginning sounds in familiar words.

9
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.580
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

10
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:50.360
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: apple, ball, cat, dog, elephant, fish.

11
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:56.160
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

12
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.860
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

13
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:09.410
The reading sequence includes Week 1: Learn the
Alphabet (A–Z) and Week 2: Phonics (Letter Sounds a–m).

14
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:10.680
Read actively.

15
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.440
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

16
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.280
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

17
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.670
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

18
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:30.790
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: A says /a/.

19
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.020
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

20
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.953
In speaking, you will complete Sound and say 1.

21
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.920
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

22
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.320
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

23
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.140
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

24
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.040
You are ready to begin.

25
00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:02.920
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

26
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.880
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

27
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.880
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
